<!--meta {"lead": "The skip link is the first thing a keyboard user reaches on every HairPop page. It jumps past the top bar straight to the content.", "description": "First focusable element on every page; hidden until focused, then shown over the top bar.", "pills": ["Native <code>&lt;a href=\"#main\"&gt;</code>", "Status: stable"], "variants": "skip to content", "states": "hidden (default), focused, hover, active", "sources": ["pages/style-gallery/default", "pages/sign-in/default", "dialogs/cancel-appointment/default"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Every page starts with <code>&lt;a class="skip-link" href="#main"&gt;Skip to content&lt;/a&gt;</code> as the first element in <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>. It stays off-screen until it receives keyboard focus, then slides into the top-left corner above the top bar. Activating it moves focus to <code>&lt;main id="main"&gt;</code>, skipping the brand, four nav links, Updates and the account link (seven tab stops on every page).</p>
  <ul>
    <li>One skip link per page, always to the main content. Add a second ("Skip to results") only for very long filter areas.</li>
    <li>It is not a replacement for landmarks and headings; pages still need them.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure">
      <a class="skip-link skip-link--demo" href="#main" data-state="focus">Skip to content</a>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 40%; top: 26%;" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 62%; top: 70%;" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
    </figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Label</b><small>"Skip to content", <code>--text-label</code>, <code>--color-fg-default</code>.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Container</b><small>Raised surface, <code>--radius-md</code>, <code>--shadow-3</code>, padding <code>--space-2</code> by <code>--space-4</code>, layer <code>--z-tooltip</code>, plus the focus ring.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  <p>One variant. <code>.skip-link--demo</code> exists only so documentation can show it in flow; never use it in product pages.</p>
  {{example:Shown as it appears when focused. On this page, press Tab once from the address bar to see the real one.}}
<a class="skip-link skip-link--demo" href="#main" data-state="focus">Skip to content</a>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes" data-na="The skip link has one size."><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <p>In product pages the default state is off-screen (<code>top: -6rem</code>); <code>:focus-visible</code> brings it to <code>--space-4</code> from the top. The demo modifier keeps it in flow so every state is visible.</p>
  <div class="ds-matrix"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Skip link</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Hover</th><th scope="col">Focus</th><th scope="col">Active</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Skip to content</th>
        <td><span class="text-muted">Off-screen; not visible</span></td>
        <td><a class="skip-link skip-link--demo" href="#main" data-state="hover">Skip to content</a></td>
        <td><a class="skip-link skip-link--demo" href="#main" data-state="focus">Skip to content</a></td>
        <td><a class="skip-link skip-link--demo" href="#main" data-state="active">Skip to content</a></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>Hover and active only happen after focus has revealed it; they use the shared link hover colour. It is never disabled.</p>
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes}}<a class="skip-link skip-link--demo" href="#main" data-state="focus">Skip to content</a>{{/themes}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The same at every width: it appears at <code>--space-4</code> from the top-left corner, over the sticky top bar.</li>
    <li>It never wraps; at 320px "Skip to content" fits with room to spare.</li>
    <li>On touch-only devices it is never seen; it is still the first element for switch and screen-reader users.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>It reads <code>--color-bg-surface-raised</code>, <code>--color-fg-default</code>, <code>--shadow-3</code> and the focus-ring tokens. In the dark theme it is grey 800 with grey 150 text and a plum 300 ring, standing out from the grey 900 top bar beneath it.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p>A native same-page link (WCAG 2.4.1 Bypass Blocks). The target is <code>&lt;main id="main"&gt;</code>; browsers move focus there when it is followed. For client-side routing, set <code>tabindex="-1"</code> on <code>main</code> and focus it in script.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd> (first press)</td><td>Focuses and reveals the skip link.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd></td><td>Moves focus to the main content; the next <kbd>Tab</kbd> lands on the first control in it.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd> (again)</td><td>Hides it and moves on to the brand in the top bar.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>The shared 2px ring plus the raised shadow make it obvious over the top bar. It sits at <code>--z-tooltip</code> so nothing covers it.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>The link text is the name: "Skip to content". Never "Skip navigation" or an icon.</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Label on raised surface|--color-fg-default|--color-bg-surface-raised|4.5}}
    {{pair:Focus ring on raised surface|--color-focus-ring|--color-bg-surface-raised|3}}
    {{pair:Focus ring on top bar|--color-focus-ring|--color-bg-surface|3}}
  </div>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>It slides down over <code>--duration-fast</code>; under reduced motion it appears instantly.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>When visible it is at least 40px tall and wide enough for its label, well above the 24px minimum.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Always "Skip to content", in sentence case.</li>
    <li>A second skip link names its target: "Skip to results".</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><a class="skip-link skip-link--demo" href="#main" data-state="focus">Skip to content</a></div><figcaption>Point it at <code>&lt;main id="main"&gt;</code> on every page, including dialogs' underlying pages.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><p class="text-muted">Dialog mocks keep the skip link active while the page behind is <code>inert</code>.</p></div><figcaption>Leave the skip link focusable while a modal dialog is open, as the dialog mocks do; it targets content that is inert. Make it inert with the page behind the dialog.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><p>Product pages reveal it only on <code>:focus-visible</code>.</p></div><figcaption>Keep it off-screen with positioning, so it stays in the accessibility tree.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><p class="text-muted"><code>display: none</code> until hover</p></div><figcaption>Hide it with <code>display: none</code> or <code>visibility: hidden</code>; it can then never receive focus.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Background|--color-bg-surface-raised}}
      {{tok:Label|--color-fg-default}}
      {{tok:Focus ring|--color-focus-ring}}
      {{tok:Shadow|--shadow-3}}
      {{tok:Radius|--radius-md}}
      {{tok:Padding|--space-2|--space-4}}
      {{tok:Visible offset / hidden offset|--space-4|--space-24}}
      {{tok:Layer|--z-tooltip}}
      {{tok:Font|--text-label}}
      {{tok:Transition|--duration-fast|--ease-standard}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;a class="skip-link" href="#main"&gt;Skip to content&lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;div class="product-shell"&gt;
    &lt;header class="topbar"&gt;…&lt;/header&gt;
    &lt;main id="main" class="container product-main" tabindex="-1"&gt;…&lt;/main&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/body&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class / attribute</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>.skip-link</code></td><td>Off-screen until <code>:focus-visible</code>, then shown top-left above everything.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>href="#main"</code></td><td>Target; <code>&lt;main&gt;</code> must carry <code>id="main"</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.skip-link--demo</code></td><td>Documentation only: keeps it in flow.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-state="focus|hover|active"</code></td><td>Documentation only: forces a state.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/style-gallery/default|first element on every page}}
    {{mock:pages/sign-in/default|auth pages}}
    {{mock:dialogs/cancel-appointment/default|stays focusable behind an open dialog}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed during extraction: in dialog mocks the skip link stays outside the <code>inert</code> page and remains focusable while the modal is open (system makes it inert with the page); the hidden offset reused <code>--space-24</code> as a magic offset (kept, documented as the hidden position).</p>
</section>
